# fixedbugs, defect 2395, lane b27-libm, 2026-11-09: a name glibc defines in
# two of its own files, bound with no `link` beside a module that links `m`,
# builds at every level.
#
# glibc defines `ldexp` in `libc.so.6` and in `libm.so.6`, both under
# `GLIBC_2.17` on Linux arm64. `pair` binds it naming no library, and
# `mathy` links `m`, so the link takes it from `libm.so.6`, which comes
# before the C library on the line, and the platform alone from
# `libc.so.6`: two files, one C library. Panel 239's R1 says glibc's pairs
# pass; until the repair this program was refused `ffi_defined_elsewhere`
# on Linux at `-O0` and `-O2`, as `libm.so.6` were another library
# interposing the C library's `ldexp`. The two files are asked the version
# each defines the name under (`cli/supplied_versions.hero`), and one
# version is one C library's.
use mathy
use pair

function main()
    print(pair.scaled())
    print(mathy.root())
